---
// How is Mon County doing? (#62, the first slice of the data dashboard in #15).
// Official numbers only, each from a file in content/indicators/ with its
// source, data year and checked date. We describe; we never say what a
// number means for policy, and never claim credit for a change.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import { loadIndicators, showValue, PLACES } from '../lib/indicators.mjs';
export const page = { door: 'community', topic: 'data', label: "How we're doing", summary: 'Official numbers on health and money in Mon County, compared with West Virginia and the US, with sources' };
const health = loadIndicators('health');
const repo = 'https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub';
---
<Base title="How is Mon County doing? Official numbers for Monongalia County, WV" description="Official numbers on child poverty, health insurance and jobs in Monongalia County, WV, next to West Virginia and the US, each with its source and year.">
  <h1>How is Mon County doing?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Official numbers about Monongalia County, next to West Virginia and the whole country. Each one links to where it comes from and says what year it covers.</p>

  <h2 id="health">Health and money</h2>
  <p>These come from <a href="https://www.countyhealthrankings.org/health-data/west-virginia/monongalia">County Health Rankings</a>, a program that gathers the same public numbers for every county in the US. We use its 2025 data file. The definitions come from its <a href="https://www.countyhealthrankings.org/sites/default/files/media/document/DataDictionary_2025.xlsx">2025 data dictionary</a>, and the years from its <a href="https://www.countyhealthrankings.org/sites/default/files/media/document/chr_trends_csv_2025.csv">2025 trends file</a>.</p>
  {health.map((i) => (
    <article class="card" id={i.slug}>
      <h3>{i.title} ({i.data_year})</h3>
      <p>{i.definition}</p>
      <ul>
        {PLACES.filter(([k]) => i.values[k] != null).map(([k, label]) => (
          <li>{k === 'monongalia' ? <strong>{label}: {showValue(i, i.values[k])}</strong> : <>{label}: {showValue(i, i.values[k])}</>}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <SourceLine sources={i.sources.slice(0, 1)} about={i.title} slug={i.slug} />
    </article>
  ))}

  <h2 id="what-it-means">What these numbers do and don't tell you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>They are for the whole county.</strong> They do not show differences between neighborhoods or towns.</li>
    <li><strong>They are estimates, and they are a year or more old.</strong> Each one says the year it covers. Small differences between places may not mean much.</li>
    <li><strong>They describe; they don't explain.</strong> A number does not say why it is high or low, or what should be done about it.</li>
    <li><strong>This site did not change them.</strong> Many people and groups shape these numbers. We only point to them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="coming">Schools and crime</h2>
  <p>We have not added official school test scores or crime numbers yet, because we could not check them on the official sources this time. That work is tracked in <a href={`${repo}/issues/772`}>issue 772</a>.</p>
</Base>
